": "Virginia's 2nd District is a rematch between incumbent Republican Jen Kiggans and former Democratic Representative Elaine Luria in an even-partisanship seat. Every major race rater now calls the district a Democratic flip, ranging from Tilt D to Likely D, and prediction markets price Luria as an overwhelming favorite. Outside groups have spent heavily against Kiggans, and the midterm environment favors the out-party.\n\nThe limited polling shows Luria narrowly ahead, and her fundraising roughly matches the incumbent's, though Kiggans holds more cash on hand. The forecast expects a Democratic win of several points, with enough residual uncertainty that a Kiggans upset cannot be fully ruled out.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7963, "margin": 4.98}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8168, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.777, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7659, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.762, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7557, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.771, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7851, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7923, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8055, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8023, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8046, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8169, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7631, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7572, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7617, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.798, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.7619, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.7517, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.7695, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.8458, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.8247, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.8351, "margin": 